{"duration_api_ms":81764,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"7940a379-0a11-4266-b3fa-1687a2479323","total_cost_usd":0.11850359999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7703,"cache_read_input_tokens":4538,"output_tokens":8678,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":6791},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7703,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8678,"cache_read_input_tokens":4538,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7703,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7703},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":8678,"cacheReadInputTokens":4538,"cacheCreationInputTokens":7703,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.11850359999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":6791,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"merged_document\":\"# Freezer Alarm Response - Night Shift\\n\\n## What triggers an alarm\\n\\nEach freezer alarms when the internal temperature rises above its set point for more than 10 minutes. The alarm sounds locally, sends a message to the night phone, and the alarm panel names the unit and shows the temperature that triggered it. Note the unit name; there are three units on this floor and two of them alarm at the same set point.\\n\\n## First response\\n\\nGo to the freezer and read the display. Write the reading and the time in the freezer log before touching anything else. The reading at the moment of arrival is the one the lab needs and it cannot be recovered later. Every alarm gets a line in the freezer log whether or not anything was wrong. An alarm with no line in the log is indistinguishable from an alarm nobody attended.\\n\\n## If the door is ajar\\n\\nRun a finger along the seal. Ice on the seal holds the door open by a few millimetres and is the usual cause of a slow rise. Close the door and wait 20 minutes. If the temperature falls back below the set point, log it as a door event and no further action is needed.\\n\\n## If the temperature keeps rising\\n\\nCall the on-call technician if the temperature is still rising 20 minutes after you arrive, and give the unit name, the reading you took on arrival, and the reading now. While waiting, do not open the door. Opening a door on a failing freezer to check the contents is the most common cause of loss in this building.\\n\\n## Moving contents\\n\\nContents are moved only on the technician's instruction and only into a freezer that already has space at the same set point. Never split a single study's samples across two freezers.\\n\\n## Weekend cover\\n\\nThe night phone is carried by the weekend duty officer from 18:00 on Friday until 08:00 on Monday.\",\"decisions\":[{\"slot\":\"title\",\"candidates\":[{\"text\":\"Freezer Alarm Response - Night Shift\",\"document\":\"source_a.md\"},{\"text\":\"Cold Storage Alarm Checklist\",\"document\":\"source_b.md\"}],\"chosen\":\"Freezer Alarm Response - Night Shift\",\"reason\":\"Base document's title is kept.\"},{\"slot\":\"heading: alarm description\",\"candidates\":[{\"text\":\"What triggers an alarm\",\"document\":\"source_a.md\"},{\"text\":\"Reading the alarm\",\"document\":\"source_b.md\"}],\"chosen\":\"What triggers an alarm\",\"reason\":\"Base heading kept; b2's content folded in as same topic.\"},{\"slot\":\"heading: door check\",\"candidates\":[{\"text\":\"If the door is ajar\",\"document\":\"source_a.md\"},{\"text\":\"Check the door seal\",\"document\":\"source_b.md\"}],\"chosen\":\"If the door is ajar\",\"reason\":\"Base heading kept; b5's seal-check content folded in.\"},{\"slot\":\"heading: escalation\",\"candidates\":[{\"text\":\"If the temperature keeps rising\",\"document\":\"source_a.md\"},{\"text\":\"Escalating\",\"document\":\"source_b.md\"}],\"chosen\":\"If the temperature keeps rising\",\"reason\":\"Base heading kept; b8's content folded in.\"},{\"slot\":\"heading: logging\",\"candidates\":[{\"text\":\"First response\",\"document\":\"source_a.md\"},{\"text\":\"Recording\",\"document\":\"source_b.md\"}],\"chosen\":\"First response\",\"reason\":\"Logging content moved into base's arrival-procedure section.\"}],\"dispositions\":[{\"segment\":\"a4\",\"disposition\":\"reconciled\",\"replacement\":\"The alarm sounds locally, sends a message to the night phone, and the alarm panel names the unit and shows the temperature that triggered it.\",\"reason\":\"Alarm sound/message combined with panel-display detail from b3.\"},{\"segment\":\"b3\",\"disposition\":\"reconciled\",\"replacement\":\"The alarm sounds locally, sends a message to the night phone, and the alarm panel names the unit and shows the temperature that triggered it.\",\"reason\":\"Panel-display fact combined with a4's alarm mechanism.\"},{\"segment\":\"b1\",\"disposition\":\"superseded\",\"replacement\":\"Freezer Alarm Response - Night Shift\",\"reason\":\"Base title chosen over this title.\"},{\"segment\":\"b2\",\"disposition\":\"superseded\",\"replacement\":\"## What triggers an alarm\",\"reason\":\"Heading consolidated under base's equivalent heading.\"},{\"segment\":\"b5\",\"disposition\":\"superseded\",\"replacement\":\"## If the door is ajar\",\"reason\":\"Heading consolidated under base's equivalent heading.\"},{\"segment\":\"b8\",\"disposition\":\"superseded\",\"replacement\":\"## If the temperature keeps rising\",\"reason\":\"Heading consolidated under base's equivalent heading.\"},{\"segment\":\"b11\",\"disposition\":\"superseded\",\"replacement\":\"## First response\",\"reason\":\"Heading consolidated under base's equivalent heading.\"},{\"segment\":\"a13\",\"disposition\":\"reconciled\",\"replacement\":\"Call the on-call technician if the temperature is still rising 20 minutes after you arrive, and give the unit name, the reading you took on arrival, and the reading now.\",\"reason\":\"General call instruction combined with b9's timing condition.\"},{\"segment\":\"b9\",\"disposition\":\"reconciled\",\"replacement\":\"Call the on-call technician if the temperature is still rising 20 minutes after you arrive, and give the unit name, the reading you took on arrival, and the reading now.\",\"reason\":\"Timing condition combined with a13's general instruction.\"},{\"segment\":\"b10\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"Call the on-call technician if the temperature is still rising 20 minutes after you arrive, and give the unit name, the reading you took on arrival, and the reading now.\",\"reason\":\"Reporting details folded into the combined call instruction.\"}],\"mismatch\":\"\"}","ttft_ms":70148,"type":"result","duration_ms":81828,"uuid":"17a01fb2-c203-4d03-a071-2a4629f64751","ttft_stream_ms":1849,"time_to_request_ms":65,"first_content_frame_ms":1849,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
